<title>SPAIN: Spain to overhaul security markets law.</title>
<headline>Spain to overhaul security markets law.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish cabinet approved on Friday an overhaul in its Security Markets Law in order to adapt it to the requirements of European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>The bill must now be approved by parliament.</p>
<p>To adapt Spanish law to Europe, foreign banks and trading houses must be allowed to operate directly in Spain.</p>
<p>Furthermore, the law would set up a guarantee fund to insure up to a maximum of 20,000 ecus in case of bankrupties.</p>
<p>The Spanish stock exchange commission CNMV would also be given additional powers.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
